Your potential, unleashed.
Indias impact on the global economy has increased at an exponential rate and Deloitte presents an opportunity to unleash and realise your potential amongst cutting edge leaders, and organisations shaping the future of the region, and indeed, the world beyond.
At Deloitte, your whole self to work, every day. Combine that with our drive to propel with purpose and you have the perfect playground to collaborate, innovate, grow, and make an impact that matters.
The team

Due diligence is now regarded as one of the most important milestones in a deal process and corporate finance.
We provide you with the opportunity to utilize your experience of commercial / strategy consulting in a challenging new environment. You will have chance to assist the world's leading investment institutions and global corporates by working on international commercial due diligence engagements as a part of Deloitte’s Global Member Firm network.
You will assist private equity, corporate, and banking clients in maximizing value from their investment and lending transactions. The Commercial Due Diligence team is a core part of Deloitte's market leading Transaction Service team and provides commercial diligence and research expertise. Widely recognised as the most experienced transactions team, we support transactions in all industry sectors, across Deloitte’s global network.

Your work profile
As an Assistant Manager in our M&A Strategy – Commercial Due Diligence Team you’ll build and nurture positive working relationships with teams and clients with the intention to exceed client expectations: -
Working as part of a larger Deloitte commercial team you will be responsible for:
Carrying out high quality research, interviews and data analysis to support either projects or business development, using tools especially MS Excel and PowerPoint;
Assisting clients in understanding the true commercial capability of acquisitions or businesses planned for disposal;
Working with corporate and private equity clients. The nature of our work varies, but chances are your engagement will involve some or all of the following topics: assessment of market condition, understanding key value drivers, review of competitive landscape, analysis of company performance, and development of strategic options;
Producing high quality input into deliverables (usually detailed written reports) within agreed timescales, briefing Partner/Director accordingly. On larger deals this will involve supporting the production of report sections together with the wider diligence team (e.g. Financial DD, Operations DD, Consulting, Tax, etc.);
Supporting various marketing initiatives and practice development activities (e.g. pitch / proposal documents development, client presentations, key client account management, industry, geography, and product programs);
Having a broader perspective of potential issues encountered when operating within diverse teams and the strategies to overcome them; and
Demonstrating M&A transaction services technical/risk management awareness and a clear understanding of the firm's commitment to creating a more inclusive culture.
Desired qualifications
Masters in Finance / MBA
We are looking for people who enjoy addressing business problems in an analytical manner, who have the patience to structure decision making, and who strive to develop pragmatic recommendations, tempered by experience. To qualify for the role ideally you would have:
Commercial due diligence or strategy consulting experience, with a strong focus on both research and reporting;
Strong commercial acumen and project management capability;
Developed your skills in a top management consultancy or a corporate environment – preferably both;
Excellent academics with a good degree or equivalent qualification as a minimum;
Structural thinking, with strong analytical and business diagnostic skills (including excel);
Experience of working in a deal environment with senior management;
Enthusiastic and positive professional attitude;
Excellent communication skills both written and oral (including PowerPoint);
A flexible approach to business demands and experience of working on short time horizons.
Excellent academic track record;
Transaction experience/exposure would be an advantage;
Strong report writing and reviewing skills, with an appropriate focus on attention to detail, conciseness and risk management;
Strong excel skills - quick and accurate manipulation of data;
Strong commercial acumen and market awareness;
Focused on high quality service; and
Fluency in written & verbal English.
Location and way of working
Base location: Mumbai
This profile involves does not involve extensive travel for work.
Hybrid is our default way of working. Each domain has customised the hybrid approach to their unique needs.

Our Harris International Group is looking to hire a Research Analyst to work closely with our Corporate Development team, M&A team and Portfolio Leader in supporting the company s mergers and acquisition (M&A) research and analysis efforts in the India.
Reporting to the Corporate Development lead, this position will play a key role in identifying, qualifying, and targeting new businesses for acquisition opportunities. You will be researching existing opportunities, finding new potential markets and verticals, researching companies for carveouts, identifying and reviewing trade show opportunities for the business development team.
The ideal candidate is someone who is comfortable working with data, has excellent technical and research skills. While no formal financial training is required, basic financial literacy and/or a software industry experience is an asset.
In this role you will be responsible for working with the portfolios M&A team to identify opportunities and software businesses that our M&A business development team will nurture.
The Role
The Research Analyst will play a key role in our capital deployment team, supporting acquisition activity by investigating opportunities based on market activity, existing databases and enhancing our M&A strategy by researching new markets and opportunities.
Maintaining and expanding the historical M&A database to ensure it reflects and provides a consistent high standard of data and analysis;
Gaining a good understanding of the markets and verticals that will help us accelerate our capital deployment
A firm understanding of our criteria to determine whether or not specific transactions meet the database inclusion criteria;
Identifying and reviewing trade show opportunities for the CD team;
Contributing to and producing reports with commentaries and data for internal publications based on our database, using specialized knowledge of M&A
Responsible for ensuring our database is updated ensure that deal records, company records and individual profiles are accurate and comprehensive;
Support the M&A team in qualifying potential company targets;
Track activities and maintain relevant information in Salesforce;
Generate and report on leads, supporting our Business development team as they set up qualified appointments and move opportunities through the M&A pipeline to our deal team.

1. POSITIONS VACANT: Consultant- Python Developer (Statistical Analysis & Data Engineering), International Not-for-Profit Organization, Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh.

2. ORGANISATIONAL BACKGROUND:
Our client is a respected international not-for-profit, that works in public health, to improve the health of disadvantaged communities, across the globe.

3. JOB DESCRIPTION/ RESPONSIBILITIES:

Reporting to the Country Lead LADS, the Consultant- Python Developer (Statistical Analysis & Data Engineering) will be based in Lucknow under multiple projects. The Consultant will optimize data pipelines for efficient data processing and conduct advanced statistical analysis with AI/ML skills. S/he will be primarily responsible for supporting various data engineering, data analysis, dashboarding, and modelling across the project.

Key Job Responsibilities:
(1) Build and optimize data pipelines for efficient data extraction, transforming/processing, and storage from various data sources;
(2) Perform data cleaning, preprocessing, data quality checks, and feature engineering to prepare datasets for modeling;
(3) Evaluate and select appropriate machine learning algorithms and techniques for specific tasks;
(4) Conduct statistical analysis on large datasets to derive actionable insights and drive decision-making. Proficiency in statistical analysis concepts such as probability distributions, hypothesis testing, regression analysis, etc. is required;
(5) Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand business requirements for analysis and translate them into technical solutions primarily dashboards and interactive analytical interfaces;
(6) Expertise and significant experience in Designing, developing, and implementing PowerBI / Tableau / Looker Studio data dashboards and data models;
(7) Familiarity with data structuring required for AI/ML models to solve complex business problems;
(8) Monitor model performance and conduct regular maintenance to ensure optimal functionality;
(9) Stay updated with the latest advancements in AI/ML technologies and contribute to innovation within the organization.

4. QUALIFICATIONS, EXPERIENCE AND COMPETENCIES:

Qualifications and Experience

(1) Bachelors or master’s degree in computer science, Data Science, Statistics, or a related field;
(2) Minimum of 2 to 3 years of experience in handling large data, analysis, and modelling;
(3) Experience in working in not-for-profit development sector in India is an added advantage;
(4) Experience in developing and deploying AI/ML models in production environments is desirable;
(5) Expertise with data engineering concepts, including ETL processes, data warehousing, and data lakes;
(6) Familiarity with ETL frameworks like Apache Spark with PySpark;
(7) Familiarity as a Python Developer with a focus on AI/ML modeling and data engineering;
(8) Knowledge of common machine learning algorithms and proficiency in implementing them using Python libraries like Scikit-learn. Understanding how to evaluate model performance using statistical metrics such as accuracy, precision, and recall is also required.

Skills and Competencies:

(1) Strong proficiency in Python programming and libraries such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, Scikit-learn, Pandas, Dask, NumPy, etc;
(2) Skilled in data visualization techniques using Python libraries such as Matplotlib, Seaborn, or Plotly;
(3) Demonstrate the ability to apply statistical analysis concepts using Python libraries like NumPy, SciPy, Pandas, etc to analyze datasets and extract meaningful insights;
(4) Solid understanding of machine learning algorithms, statistical methods, and data structures;
(5) Proficiency in developing dashboards using commonly available platforms like PowerBI and Looker Studio;
(6) Development capability in PowerApps and/or Firebase is a plus;
(7) Proficiency in SQL and relational database management systems (e.g., MySQL, PostgreSQL);
(8) Knowledge of cloud environments and usage of tools AWS, Azure, etc.;
(9) Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to work independently or in a team environment;
(10) Strong communication and interpersonal skills can explain complex technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders;
(11) Willing to travel to program sites in Rajasthan and Uttar Pradesh and excited to get on the ground.

5. CONSULTANCY FEE: The consultancy fee budgeted for the assignment is in the range of INR 60,000 to 1,50,000 per month.

6. LOCATION: Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh

7. NATURE OF CONTRACT:

The selected candidate shall be engaged as a Consultant on the rolls of SAMS, a third-party payrolling agency, for a full-time consultancy engagement initially offered for a period of three to eight months. The contract is extendable based on performance and project requirements. It is explicitly clarified that this consultancy engagement does not constitute a promise or guarantee of future employment, with SAMS, or our client, or any other organization associated with the project.
8. REFERENCE: CPD-INPO
9. CONTACT INFORMATION:

